'''Fuzzball''' was a small [[Color|orange]]-haired [[Species|creature]] belonging to a furry, fluttering<ref name="Fuzzball DB" /> [[Fuzzball (species)|species of the same name]].<ref name="Way Way Out AD" /> During the [[New Republic Era]], Fuzzball and other members of his species were captured by [[pirate]]s and caged at a pet store in the [[shadowport]] of [[Borgo Prime]].<ref name="Fuzzball DB" /> Around the [[Standard year|year]] [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{SkeletonCrewDate}}</ref> a group of children from the [[planet]] [[At Attin]] found themselves lost on Borgo. While looking for directions back home, one of the children, [[KB]], encountered Fuzzball and shared a friendly moment with him. Later, during a skirmish with a [[Silvo's pirates|pirate crew]], KB's [[droid]] companion [[SM-33]] threw a [[Unidentified Warthog alien|Warthog attacker]] into the pet shop, knocking the cages open and freeing Fuzzball and the others of his kind.<ref name="Way Way Out">{{SkeletonCrew|Way, Way Out Past the Barrier}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Fuzzball's first appearance in [[canon]] ''[[Star Wars]]'' media occurred with the release of "[[Way, Way Out Past the Barrier]]," the second episode of the [[2024]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]''.<ref name="Way Way Out" /> Prior to that, the character originated in [[Wikipedia:Captain EO|''Captain EO'']], a [[1986]] science fiction musical short film. Written by [[George Lucas]], the now-defunct ''Captain EO'' was featured as an attraction in [[The Walt Disney Company|Walt Disney Parks]].<ref name="Way Way Out Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/skeleton-crew/season-1-episode-2-episode-guide|text="Way, Way Out Past the Barrier" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars: Skeleton Crew}}</ref> In ''Skeleton Crew'', sounds for Fuzzball were provided by voice talent [[Shelby Young]] and [[Terri Douglas]]. [[Skywalker Sound]], having worked on the original attraction, provided access to archival recordings of Fuzzball for the actors to base their performances on.<ref name="Strange and Familiar">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-skywalker-sound-interview|text=The Strange and Familiar Sounds of ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew''}}</ref>

